<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Obersontheim</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Obersontheim is a village in the district of Schwäbisch Hall in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. In the early modern period it was the residence of the Limpurg-Sontheim branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schenk-von-limpurg">Schenks of Limpurg</a>, whose castle survives. After the family died out in 1713 it passed to their heirs, and in 1806 it became part of Württemberg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/obersontheim.jpg" alt="Obersontheim" width="320" height="302" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagar66 based on work of TUBS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Obersontheim_in_SHA.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
